      "points": [
       "The mature phase of the Harappan civilisation is dated to about 2600–1900 BCE.",
       "In 1921, Daya Ram Sahni began excavations at Harappa (on the Ravi, Punjab).",
       "In 1922, R.D. Banerji discovered Mohenjodaro (on the Indus).",
       "In 1924, John Marshall formally announced the discovery of the Indus Valley Civilisation.",
       "Town planning features: grid-pattern streets, covered drains, a citadel and a lower town.",
       "The Great Bath at Mohenjodaro was a rectangular watertight tank made of bricks.",
       "Lothal (Gujarat) has yielded a dockyard, and Kalibangan (Rajasthan) evidence of a ploughed field.",
       "The Harappan script remains undeciphered; steatite seals often show the unicorn animal.",
       "The Harappan civilisation is divided into Early (c. 3200–2600 BCE), Mature (2600–1900 BCE) and Late (c. 1900–1300 BCE) phases.",
       "Charles Masson first noticed Harappa's ruins in 1826; Alexander Cunningham visited the site in 1875.",
       "Harappa's baked bricks were carted off as ballast for the Lahore–Multan railway line.",
       "The five major Harappan cities were Mohenjodaro, Harappa, Ganweriwala, Rakhigarhi and Dholavira.",
       "Rakhigarhi (Hisar, Haryana) is the largest known Harappan site.",
       "Dholavira (Kutch, Gujarat) had huge water reservoirs and a town divided into three parts.",
       "Terracotta models of the plough from Banawali (Haryana) and Kalibangan show the plough was used in farming.",
       "Chanhudaro (Sindh) was a famous bead-making centre with workshops for making seals.",
       "Evidence of millets like bajra and jowar comes from Rangpur and Rojdi in Gujarat.",
       "Shortughai (Afghanistan) was a Harappan trading outpost for lapis lazuli.",
       "Mesopotamian texts call the Indus region 'Meluhha'; Dilmun and Magan were trading partners.",
       "Harappan weights were made of chert and standardised, following a binary ratio (1, 2, 4, 8...).",
       "Almost every house at Mohenjodaro had a well, and bathrooms drained into covered street drains.",
       "The steatite 'Priest King' statue and the bronze 'Dancing Girl' (lost-wax method) come from Mohenjodaro.",
       "The Pashupati seal shows a yogi surrounded by elephant, tiger, rhinoceros and buffalo — regarded as proto-Shiva.",
       "Terracotta mother-goddess figurines are abundant; tree and animal worship is also attested.",
       "No conclusive evidence of the horse has been found; cattle, buffalo, goat and sheep were domesticated.",
       "The dead were buried extended, head to the north; Harappa's cemeteries reveal social differences."
      ],
