       "Ibn Battuta (14th century) was a Moroccan traveller; he wrote the 'Rihla' in Arabic.",
       "Ibn Battuta became the qazi of Delhi during the reign of Muhammad bin Tughlaq.",
       "Francois Bernier (1656–68), a French physician, stayed at the Mughal court and served Dara Shukoh.",
       "Bernier wrote 'Travels in the Mughal Empire'; he proposed the theory of crown ownership of land.",
       "Al-Biruni (973–1048) was a scholar from Khwarizm (Uzbekistan) who came to India with Mahmud of Ghazni.",
       "Al-Biruni learnt Sanskrit and translated Patanjali's grammar; his Kitab-ul-Hind is in Arabic.",
       "Kitab-ul-Hind has 80 chapters — on religion, philosophy, customs, law and astronomy.",
       "Al-Biruni criticised the caste system and child marriage, and praised Indian sciences (mathematics, astronomy).",
       "Ibn Battuta (1304–1377) was a Moroccan traveller; his Rihla is an Arabic travelogue.",
       "Ibn Battuta reached India in 1333; Muhammad bin Tughlaq appointed him the qazi of Delhi.",
       "Tughlaq sent Ibn Battuta as his envoy to China.",
       "Ibn Battuta described paan, coconut, the postal system (ulug/dawa), bazaars and sati.",
       "Francois Bernier (1620–1688) was a French physician in India from 1656–1668, attached to Dara Shukoh's court.",
       "Bernier's 'Travels in the Mughal Empire' is dedicated to Louis XIV of France.",
       "Bernier claimed crown ownership of land in Mughal India — no private property, hence no progress.",
       "Montesquieu built his 'oriental despotism' theory on Bernier; Marx's Asiatic mode of production was also influenced.",
