       "Marco Polo passed through South India; Duarte Barbosa was a Portuguese traveller.",
       "Travellers' accounts have limits — language barriers, bias, exaggeration — and must be cross-checked with other sources.",
       "Al-Biruni noted Indian society was divided into castes with special honour for Brahmanas.",
       "Ibn Battuta's account reflects the administrative system and urban prosperity of the Delhi Sultanate."
